WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:17.278
Mark: Poor Jim. That tree smashed his house!

2
00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:22.810
Woman: It happened during the windstorm.

3
00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:25.769
Coby: I hope everybody is okay.

4
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:33.236
Mark: Me too.

5
00:00:33.237 --> 00:00:36.068
Daisy: Did you see Jim's house?

6
00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:39.353
Maya: Yes. It got crushed!

7
00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:42.539
Kara: I heard his whole house is ruined.

8
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.935
Mark: Miss Gray, is Jim coming to school today?

9
00:00:45.936 --> 00:00:49.005
Miss Gray: Please put away your things and come to the rug.

10
00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:53.168
Miss Gray: Then we'll talk about Jim.

11
00:00:53.169 --> 00:00:55.675
Coby: Do you know if Jim is okay?

12
00:00:55.676 --> 00:00:57.881
Mark: We went to his house yesterday.

13
00:00:57.882 --> 00:01:00.100
But nobody was there.

14
00:01:00.101 --> 00:01:03.069
Miss Gray: Jim and his family are fine.

15
00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.872
Class: Whew!

16
00:01:04.873 --> 00:01:05.935
Miss Gray: They're lucky.

17
00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:07.469
No one was hurt.

18
00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.474
Miss Gray: But it will take time to fix their house.

19
00:01:10.475 --> 00:01:12.484
Mark: Where's Jim now?

20
00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:15.600
Miss Gray: He's staying with his grandmother.

21
00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:19.516
Mark: When will he be back?

22
00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:21.619
Miss Gray: She lives far away.

23
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.146
Miss Gray: So he probably won't be back until next week.

24
00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:28.946
Miss Gray: The rain ruined a lot of his family's things.

25
00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:30.618
Jenna: His books?

26
00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:32.849
Mark: His video games?

27
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.804
Kara: His clothes?

28
00:01:35.805 --> 00:01:40.624
Miss Gray: Everything. Later we can make some cards for Jim.

29
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:43.404
Miss Gray: That way he'll know we're thinking about him.

30
00:01:43.405 --> 00:01:51.172
Class: Okay. Good idea!

31
00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:54.270
Mark: Mom, I feel sad about Jim.

32
00:01:54.271 --> 00:01:58.009
Mark: His house won't be fixed for a long time.

33
00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:01.434
Mrs. Conlan: Yes. And they lost a lot of things.

34
00:02:01.435 --> 00:02:08.716
Mrs. Conlan: His family will need help from their friends.

35
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:10.752
Mark: I'm Jim's friend.

36
00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:14.499
Maybe I can help!
